Theorem RL-101: Parser soundness round-trip

  Preconditions:
    - f is a file accepted by aims-proof/checker/src/parser.rs::parse_proof_file
    - tokens is the token stream produced by tokenize per
      the canonical proof notation sec-Notation-Parseability
    - ast is parse_proof_file_tokens_with_source tokens f produced
      ProofFile structure per aims-proof/checker/src/ast.rs
    - reparse f re-runs parse_proof_file_tokens_with_source on the same
      source and yields a ProofFile of the identical AST shape
    - the kernel surface comprises parser.rs and ast.rs and the
      dispatch loop in checker.rs per the proof-checker design sec-Kernel-Verification-Methodology

  Soundness property:
    Forall f in CanonicalNotationFile.
      parse_proof_file f succeeds implies
        reparse f preserves every Theorem id and every Theorem
        soundness source and every Theorem proof obligation step
        source modulo whitespace normalization;
      i.e. no theorem accepted by the parser is dropped or renamed on
        re-parse; the AST is total over its accepted input domain.

  Proof obligation:
    Structural induction over ProofFile.theorems and per-theorem
    sub-block enumeration.

      Base case: ProofFile with zero theorems.
        parser rejects an empty theorem list per parse_proof_file_tokens_with_source
        emitting NotationMissingTheoremBlock; the success branch is
        never reached on a zero-theorem file because the parser returns
        an error BEFORE producing an AST.

      Inductive step: ProofFile with N theorems implies the same
      property holds at N + 1.
        Assume the property holds for the first N theorems.
        For the (N + 1) theorem t:
          (a) t.id has a category prefix and numeric suffix per
              parse_theorem_id; category_from_prefix returns Some on
              every prefix the lexer can produce given category_word
              keyword classification.
          (b) t.preconditions is a list of bullets read by
              parse_preconditions; the bullets are preserved verbatim
              in the AST.
          (c) t.soundness.source is a verbatim canonical-notation
              string read by parse_soundness via read_indented_body;
              the string is preserved verbatim in the AST.
          (d) t.obligation is either ProofObligation::Sorry or
              ProofObligation::Steps with a single opaque step source;
              both shapes are preserved in the AST; no proof obligation
              text is dropped.
          (e) t.expected is preserved verbatim; the Expected status and
              reason are retained in the AST, matching the .expected
              golden file shape.

      Closed-world coverage:
        Every Token variant produced by tokenize maps to a parser
        sub-block consumer; no parser-accepted input falls off the
        parse dispatch.

    Lattice validation:
      Parser-soundness is a structural property; lattice dimensions
      do not participate. The kernel invariant under verification is
      that every accepted input is faithfully reproduced on re-parse.

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (over ProofFile.theorems and per-theorem
                            sub-blocks)
      case_analysis (per Token variant enumeration; per ProofObligation
                     variant enumeration; per Expected key enumeration)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: 01A bootstrap discharged via §01A Implementation Items (engine constructive verification + Lean 4 cross-validation)
